## 8. Database Design

A central SQLite database will store the information collected from both devices.

### Planned Tables

| Table             | Important fields                                                        |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `users`           | user_id, username, settings                                             |
| `devices`         | device_id, device_type, device_name                                     |
| `games`           | game_id, game_name, package_name, executable_name                       |
| `gaming_sessions` | session_id, user_id, device_id, game_id, start_time, end_time, duration |
| `watch_readings`  | reading_id, timestamp, heart_rate, hrv, activity                        |
| `stress_results`  | result_id, timestamp, estimated_score, model_version                    |
| `alerts`          | alert_id, alert_type, message, timestamp                                |
| `settings`        | setting_id, gaming_limit, stress_threshold, notification_preferences    |

The `device_type` field will distinguish Windows sessions from Android sessions.

Each session will have a unique identifier to avoid duplicate records during synchronization.

