## 9. Local Communication and Synchronization

The Windows laptop will host the backend.

Example local network configuration:

```text
Laptop IP:       192.168.1.5
Backend Port:    8000
Backend URL:     http://192.168.1.5:8000
```

These are example values. The actual laptop IP address will be determined during setup.

### Communication Flow

1. Windows application records a gaming session.
2. Windows application uploads the record to FastAPI.
3. Android application records mobile gaming sessions.
4. Android application uploads records when the server is reachable.
5. FastAPI stores both types of sessions in SQLite.
6. Dashboard retrieves combined information.
7. Machine-learning services analyze suitable data.
8. Reports are generated from the central database.

### Offline Synchronization

The Android app will store unsynchronized sessions locally.

When the laptop backend becomes available, the app will upload pending records.

The backend will use unique session identifiers to prevent duplicate records.

